# Demo app config for E2E tests — production bridge backend.
# Loaded by `vite dev --mode test.prod`, i.e. `bun run test:e2e:prod`.
#
# Tracked in git on purpose: it holds no secrets, and a clean checkout has to be
# able to run the prod suite without anyone hand-writing a file first (TBP-606).
#
# NOTE: No auth/cloud-views URLs set — the plugin resolves production
# endpoints automatically. This mirrors the real user experience.
#
# Resolved by `e2e/playwright/global-setup.ts` from the prod test-data API and
# seeded into localStorage as `bridge:appId`, which `demo/src/routes/+layout.ts`
# prefers over this variable. Deliberately EMPTY rather than absent: Vite falls
# a MISSING key through to `demo/.env.local`, a developer's untracked local file
# that pins a slot-0 app id — the same fall-through that pointed the stage run
# at a localhost portal (TBP-607). To serve this demo by hand outside Playwright,
# put a prod app id here.
VITE_BRIDGE_APP_ID=

# VITE_ENVIRONMENT=prod also makes `+layout.ts` skip the apiBaseUrl/hostedUrl
# overrides entirely, so the SDK resolves its own production endpoints — which
# is why no VITE_BRIDGE_HOSTED_URL is needed here. It is additionally what the
# demo's AppShell env pill shows, and global-setup asserts that pill against the
# Playwright project so a demo left running in the wrong `--mode` fails loudly.
VITE_ENVIRONMENT=prod
VITE_BRIDGE_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:3008/auth/oauth-callback
VITE_BRIDGE_DEBUG=true
